  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The white precipitate silver chloride is soluble in ammonia and forms the complex with coordination number 2. The complex formation is shown below.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AgCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8594;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>Ag</mi><msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>Cl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>It is ammoniacal silver chloride.&nbsp;</p>"
